<title>USA: Ogilvy &amp; Mather to buy Denison Bates of Brazil.</title>
<headline>Ogilvy &amp; Mather to buy Denison Bates of Brazil.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ogilvy &amp; Mather Worldwide said Wednesday it was acquiring Denison Bates Advertising in Sao Paulo, Brazil.</p>
<p>Denison Bates will be merged with Ogilvy's existing wholly owned advertising agency, Standard, Ogilvy &amp; Mather, to become the largest agency in Brazil in terms of media buying, Ogilvy said.</p>
<p>Total billings are estimated by Ad Age's 1995 Agency Report to be $268 million, Ogilvy said.</p>
<p>Terms of the acquisition were not disclosed.</p>
<p>Ogilvy, a unit of WPP Group PLC, said this was its first major acquisition of the decade.</p>
